meta {
  name: Get
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/rapportage/verkoop-fur
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.items: isArray
  res.body.periodeVan: isDefined
  res.body.periodeTot: isDefined
  res.body.generatedAt: isDefined
}

docs {
  Verkoop FUR dealer overview - Nomaled dealers (klant.swNomaled = TRUE)
  who ordered a "FUR spot" article (bonlijn.artnr BEGINS "NOMALED.FUR")
  in the rolling 12-months window (TODAY - 365 .. TODAY, both bounds
  inclusive).

  Response shape:
  {
    "items": [
      { "klnr": 14644, "naam": "CONE LIGHTING BV", "aantalFurOrders": 3,
        "totaalAantalStuks": 42, "laatsteBesteldatum": "2026-07-15" },
      ...
    ],
    "periodeVan": "2025-08-20",
    "periodeTot": "2026-08-20",
    "generatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:15:03..."
  }

  Sorted `items` BY totaalAantalStuks DESCENDING (Marc-confirmed - see
  docs/architecture/verkoop-fur-ontwerp.md Open flags #3, overrides the
  architect's original laatsteBesteldatum suggestion).

  Business rules baked into this result (see
  Luna.BusinessLogic.VerkoopFurBE class header for the full rationale):
  - bon.type must be "ORDERBEVESTIGING".
  - Cancelled-order heuristic: bon.b-bedrag = 0 -> excluded (annul-bon
    always zeroes this; accepted false-positive/false-negative risk per
    Marc, see design doc Open flags #1).
  - Only bon.klnr (primary) is attributed - klnr2/klnr3 are not
    considered.
  - naam is klant.naam (live/current), not a point-in-time snapshot.
  - Not cached - this endpoint always recomputes live, generatedAt is
    always "now".

  Backed by Backend/src/Luna/Web/RapportageHandler.cls +
  Luna/BusinessLogic/VerkoopFurBE.cls. Read-only, no auth (consistent
  with every other documented handler).
}
